# Airdrop — the Launch distributor for the root token.
#
# The contract is the canonical share-based Merkle airdrop from LOVE20TKM/burn (vendored into
# src/vendor/Airdrop.sol with its origin commit recorded there). Its constructor takes five
# immutables: sourceChainId, sourceBlockNumber, sourceBurnAddress, merkleRoot, totalShare.
#
# The merkle root and totalShare are NOT written here: they are derived data, so they live in the
# snapshot that script/gen_airdrop_fixture.py generates (fixtures/airdrop/anvil31337_dev.json), and
# DeployLocal.s.sol reads them from that file. Keeping one copy means a stale param cannot disagree
# with the proofs the frontend is served. This file pins the PROVENANCE metadata that is baked into
# the contract, plus the snapshot path, and DeployLocal asserts the two agree:
#   sourceChainId  == snapshot.sourceChainId
#   sourceBlockNumber == snapshot.sourceBlockNumber
#   sourceBurnAddress == snapshot.sourceBurnAddress
#   merkleRoot    == snapshot.merkleRoot
#   totalShare    == snapshot.totalShare
#
# The provenance values are synthetic and say so: this local chain has no Burn deployment, so there
# is no real burn activity to snapshot. They are non-zero (the contract rejects zero) and unique to
# this profile (31337 / 1 / a clearly fake burn address) so nobody mistakes them for mainnet data.
SOURCE_CHAIN_ID=31337
SOURCE_BLOCK_NUMBER=1
SOURCE_BURN_ADDRESS=0x00000000000000000000000000000000C0FFEE01
AIRDROP_SNAPSHOT_FILE=fixtures/airdrop/anvil31337_dev.json
# 1e18 == 100% of the distributable share; the vendored contract rejects 0 and >1e18.
TOTAL_SHARE=1e18
# The launch distributor is the Airdrop contract itself; Launch mints LAUNCH_AMOUNT to it in the
# LOVE20Token constructor. This is wired programmatically by DeployLocal.s.sol (the address only
# exists at run time), so there is no DISTRIBUTOR_ADDRESS key to get stale.
#
# The vendored Airdrop does NOT implement ILaunchDistributor (no onTokenLaunched callback) - verified
# by compiling and by `cast call` in script/verify.sh. Child-token launches therefore must use
# DistributorMode.NoCallback on this chain; documented in README "Known limitations".
